  "releaseNotes": "2.1.1: Made Core.Idempotency.Constants.HeaderNames public so consumers can reference the well-known idempotency header names instead of hardcoding string literals.\n\t\t\t2.1.0: Multi-targeting release. The package now ships net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0 assets instead of net8.0 only, so a project on .NET 9 or .NET 10 gets an assembly compiled for its own target framework.\n\t\t\tDependency refresh. No code or API changes.\n\t\t\tCoreSystem.Observability.Abstractions 1.0.1 to 1.0.2,\n\t\t\tCoreSystem.Serialization 1.2.3 to 1.2.4 and\n\t\t\tOpenTelemetry.Extensions.Hosting 1.19.0 to 1.20.0, plus the refreshed\n\t\t\ttransitive graph. The declared dependency floors now match the versions\n\t\t\tthe assembly was built and tested against.",
